Extender FILEMGR find-first CARRY-FLAG chain: 89b0's four .MEG RAM-size probes
must leave the detail/LOD word [0x8490] at the TCB base (TCB+0x59 = 0x0b) but
Ghidra dropped the x86 CF at every level of the find chain, so every probe read
"found" and bumped detail 0x0b -> 0xc (=> a 4096x4096 = 8 MB heightmap instead of
2048x2048 = 2 MB, the bc06 LOD-upsampler heap overflow).

Root cause (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_image.bin): the extender find chain
    89b0 -> 5c98 -> 5cc2 -> 5d50 -> 6250
signals found (clc, CF=0) vs not-found (stc, CF=1) purely through the x86 CF.
The __allregs model returns AX/void, not flags, so:
  * 5c98's `in_CF` was hardcoded 0 -> always returned 0xffffffff "found";
  * 5d50 was `void` (dropped its own clc/stc AND 6250's bVar6);
  * 5cc2's bVar3 was hardcoded false;
  * 89b0's uVar10 was hardcoded 0 -> `if(!(bool)uVar10)` always taken -> bump.
The real 4E find-first result IS computed correctly in 5d50 (uRam000f0012 = the
shim R_CF after fist_int_dispatch); it was just never propagated up.

asm ground truth (objdump re_out/fist_image.bin):
    89b0 probe : 89e7 call 5c98 ; 89ec jb <skip> ; 89f5 mov [0x8490],N   (bump on CF CLEAR)
    5c98       : 5ca0 call 5cc2 ; 5ca5 jb 5cae ; (found) eax=-1,clc ; (nf) eax=0,stc
    5cc2       : 5d1f call 5d50 ; 5d24 jae 5d4f(found->ret CF=0) ; ... 5d4e stc(nf)
    5d50       : 5df4 int21 ; 5df8 jae 5e19(found) ; 5e10 call 6250 ; 5e34 clc(found) 5e38 stc(nf)
    6250       : 63ca/638f clc(found) ; 63f6 stc(nf) ; 641b fatal->nf

Fix: thread the CF through a dedicated shim global `g_ext_find_cf`
(tools/native_main.c), written at each function's clc/stc and read by its caller
in the exact synchronous call order (no engine code runs between producer and
consumer in this extender-local chain, so a single global is exact).  Distinct
from g_fist_cf (the engine seg-0 paint CF).

DUAL-PATH: this chain is SHARED with the default-boot KDV intro (TITLE.KDV find-
first).  For a file that EXISTS the 4E succeeds (CF clear at 5d50's int) -> the
success branch is taken without ever calling 6250 -> g_ext_find_cf=0 (found),
unchanged behaviour.  Only the failing .MEG probes now correctly flip to CF=1.
Validated: default boot plays the KDV intro (395 frames, rc=0) AND the mission
cascade keeps detail=0x0b.  Flat32-module dropped-CARRY class; never exercised
before op-0x18 (89b0) reached the .MEG probes.

